WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.400
Windows systems organize evidence across standard locations, user-specific areas, protected directories, and application data stores.

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:17.817
The Windows directory, especially C:\Windows and C:\Windows\System32, contains operating system components, drivers, configuration, logs, and administrative utilities.

00:00:17.817 --> 00:00:26.726
Analysts should treat these locations carefully because normal system activity and updates can create many changes.

00:00:26.726 --> 00:00:31.053
User profiles are usually found under C:\Users.

00:00:31.053 --> 00:00:44.543
A profile can contain documents, desktop items, downloads, browser data, application settings, jump lists, shortcuts, recent file traces, cloud sync artifacts, and user-specific registry hives.

00:00:44.543 --> 00:00:54.470
Profiles are central to user activity reconstruction, but they do not automatically prove who physically performed an action.

00:00:54.470 --> 00:01:01.343
Shared systems, remote access, service accounts, and compromised credentials can complicate attribution.

00:01:01.343 --> 00:01:07.197
Program Files and Program Files x86 commonly contain installed applications.

00:01:07.197 --> 00:01:13.560
ProgramData often stores shared application data, logs, configuration, and updater artifacts.

00:01:13.560 --> 00:01:21.451
Temp directories may contain short-lived files, installers, scripts, extracted archives, or application working data.

00:01:21.451 --> 00:01:29.341
The recycle bin may preserve deleted file references and metadata depending on the scenario.

00:01:29.341 --> 00:01:33.668
Hidden and protected files can also matter.

00:01:33.668 --> 00:01:35.959
System context matters.

00:01:35.959 --> 00:01:45.886
A domain-joined workstation, kiosk, server, cloud instance, developer machine, and shared jump host all produce different evidence patterns.

00:01:45.886 --> 00:01:57.849
Analysts should identify the system role, operating system version, installed security tools, time zone, user population, and logging configuration before drawing conclusions.

00:01:57.849 --> 00:02:05.740
The layout gives a map, but context tells the analyst where to look first.
